	(text "USB CONNECTOR"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 115.062 33.274 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(thickness 0.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a7dfa0e5-5bf7-4c52-a76f-c06e67b78415")
	)
	(text "D+/D- go straight from connector to MCU, only the USBLC6 in between:\n  - no series resistors: internal impedance driver (AN4879 sec 3.1)\n  - no 1k5 pull-up on D+: built into the F405 (DS8626 sec 3.30, tab 58)\n  - no capacitors on the data lines\n\nCC1 and CC2 each get their OWN 5k1 to GND. Never tie them:\nbreaks orientation detection and conflicts with VCONN on\ne-marked cables. Without them, a USB-C host won't enable VBUS.\n\nVBUS must not go straight to PA9. Vmax = VDD+4V (DS8626 tab 11);\nwith the board unpowered the limit drops to 4V. 33k/82k divider\ngives ~3.57V at the pin (AN4879 sec 2.6.1).\n>> FIRMWARE: do not set OTG_GCCFG.VBDEN. PA9 is a plain GPIO,\n   no pull-up, no pull-down.\n\nDivider taps VBUS_RAW, BEFORE D4. On +5V it would read 5V\nwhenever the PDB is on, and the signal would be meaningless.\n\nD4 lets the board run from USB on the bench and keeps the PDB\nBEC from backfeeding the host port. Budget: 500mA after\nenumeration, 100mA before. Total VBUS capacitance <= 10uF.\n\nR12 (10k) bleeds D4 reverse leakage. Without it, the leakage flows\nthrough the 115k divider and firmware reads \"host present\" in flight."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 100.838 60.198 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d99c03c5-9794-42ad-8f42-36d9f63c28aa")
	)
